---
// The agent's request path (#18, how-this-works page). An HTML diagram, not a bitmap: every label is
// real text. Two lanes show the boundary that matters most: pages never reach the Worker.
---

<figure class="editorial-diagram request-path" aria-labelledby="request-path-caption">
  <div class="request-path__lanes">
    <div class="request-path__lane">
      <p class="request-path__lane-label">Every page</p>
      <p class="request-path__route"><code>/</code>, <code>/work/</code>, <code>/writing/</code> …</p>
      <p>Served as files straight from the build. No code of mine runs, so reading the site never touches the agent.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="request-path__lane request-path__lane--agent">
      <p class="request-path__lane-label">Agent requests only</p>
      <p class="request-path__route"><code>/agent/*</code>, same origin as the pages</p>
      <ol class="request-path__steps">
        <li><span class="request-path__step-name">Guard</span> One shared object checked first: blocklist, daily count, paused-until.</li>
        <li><span class="request-path__step-name">Your session</span> One per visitor, named by the server, with its own conversation storage.</li>
        <li><span class="request-path__step-name">Two read-only tools</span> Search the corpus and read one source from it.</li>
        <li><span class="request-path__step-name">Model</span> Workers AI, called through AI Gateway, where the spend limit lives.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="request-path-caption">
    One origin, two lanes. Pages are files; only <code>/agent/*</code> reaches the Worker, and each agent request passes
    the guard before it reaches a session or the model.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .request-path {
    margin: 2rem 0 2.25rem;
  }
  .request-path__lanes {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .request-path__lanes {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 3fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
  .request-path__lane {
    border: 1px solid var(--editorial-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
  }
  .request-path__lane--agent {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .request-path__lane p {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .request-path .request-path__lane-label {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--fg);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .request-path .request-path__route {
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .request-path__steps {
    counter-reset: request-step;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .request-path__steps li {
    counter-increment: request-step;
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 2.25rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  /* The number carries order and sits on the item's first line. */
  .request-path__steps li::before {
    content: counter(request-step, decimal-leading-zero);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.2rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .request-path__step-name {
    display: block;
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .request-path figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
</style>
